<a href="https://store.greaterthangames.com/sentinels-of-the-multiverse-core-game.html?category_id=9">https://store.greaterthangames.com/sentinels-of-the-multiverse-core-game.html?category_id=9</a>

&nbsp;

When we say it&rsquo;s ended it just means that Greater than Games is no longer going to make any more expansions for it. &nbsp; It&rsquo;s a complete and huge game with a ton of expansions and replayabilty. &nbsp; It&rsquo;s not gonna fade away anytime soon.&nbsp;

Instead they are going to be licensing the card system out to other companies to make games(like Sentnels of Earth Prime) and working in other games both in the universe(Prime War(a tactical games), &nbsp;the RPG and some other projects)) as well as games not tied to Sentinels Comics. &nbsp;

It&rsquo;s really a great game with a tone of lore. &nbsp;The head writer and artist to a really fun podcast where they discuss the lore in detail which is also worth a listen if those are your thing.&nbsp;

[quote="The Mariner"]

Fortunately, there&rsquo;s a thriving <strong>homebrew</strong> community already, and even when Christoper&rsquo;s suddenly-cosmonautical brain runs out of new ideas, that<strong> homebrew</strong> community will pick up where the official content left off, probably to slow-claps. &nbsp;Maybe not all the <strong>homebrew</strong> stuff is as good, but a lot of homebrewers pride themselves on throughly testing their content (myself included, which is why none of you knew about my secret until now), and the Sentinels engine will be able to coast for at least a decade.

&nbsp;

TL;DR- Yeah, I think it&rsquo;s worth the investment. &nbsp;That said, Adam would probably appreciate if you waited for the new art version.

[/quote]

